cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SafeAgentEval or SafeOrderBench, please cite it as below."
title: "SafeAgentEval and SafeOrderBench: State-Verified Safety Evaluation for Transactional AI Agents"
authors:
  - name: "Cirigiri, Rammohan Srikanth"
version: 0.2.0
date-released: 2026-11-09
license: CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  An open-source framework and standardized benchmark for evaluating whether
  AI agents executing consumer transactions act within their authorized
  mandate and report their actions truthfully. The released benchmark is a
  16-scenario banking/payments pack in seven safety categories, graded by
  final state, reply-content constraints, and claim verification over a
  hash-linked trace, in black-box (session-agent) execution mode.
keywords:
  - ai-agents
  - safety-evaluation
  - agentic-payments
  - benchmark
